        // But we don't have the old balance stored. So we read it from mapping before burn is impossible after set up.
        // Instead, we rely on the fact that the reference satisfies: balanceOf[caller] before burn >= burnValue, and after burn it is balance_before - burnValue.
        // To avoid storing, we can use a different approach: after burn, balanceOf[caller] + burnValue == balanceOf[caller] before burn (but we can't read before).
        // So we can do a two-step: first read balance, then burn, then check difference.
        // But that would require storing in a local variable, which is fine.
        uint256 balanceBefore = c.balanceOf(caller);
